T SeamSpecification                   | SeamSpecification.h | 59-121 | owning                        | -  | One surface's seams, both sources held apart because they have different lifetimes. discarded by a re-unwrap. An artist who spent an hour marking seams and watched an automatic partition erase them has lost work the program told them it was holding. next partition. Where a surface will not flatten within the declared distortion using the authored set alone, the shortfall is cut and the addition is reported through `86` — a silent extra cut is a seam the artist finds later in the painted result.
